course: dictionary
lesson: 737
title: Baskets make equal groups
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A basket is a container made of woven strips, used to carry things like fruit or bread. In maths, think of each basket as one equal group, with the same number of things inside.
explain: «4 baskets, 2 three-pointers and 3 free throws» uses baskets to count points. Each basket is worth 2 points here, so 4 baskets make 4 × 2 = 8 points. The number of baskets times the points in each basket gives the total.
explain: If you have baskets with the same number in each, you multiply to find the total. If you put a total into baskets equally, you divide to find how many go in each basket.
fact: A basket is a container made of woven strips, used to carry things like fruit or bread.
fact: In basketball, the basket is the net the ball goes through, and each basket made is a score.
fact: A shopping basket is what you put things in at a shop or online.
fact: «Baskets with N in each» means multiply: the total is the number of baskets times N.
fact: «Put into baskets equally» means divide: share the total so every basket has the same amount.
exercise: There are 4 baskets with 5 apples in each. How many apples in total? | 54 | 9 | 45 | *20
exercise: A player makes 3 baskets, each worth 2 points. How many points is that? | 32 | *6 | 2 | 5
exercise: You put 12 plums into 3 baskets equally. How many plums go in each basket? | *4 | 6 | 9 | 3
test: Mum's «shopping basket» has 6 items that each cost 2 pounds. How much does the basket cost? | *12 | 6 | 4 | 8
test: You share 24 eggs equally into 4 baskets. How many eggs are in each basket? | 4 | 20 | *6 | 8
exam: There are 5 baskets with 3 plums in each, and 2 plums are eaten. How many plums are left? | 10 | *13 | 7 | 15
